 ## Overview
-This method computes the initial microflake parameters—density $\rho_0$ and self-shadowing $A_0$—for a low-resolution voxel such that its directional transparencies match those of the input high-resolution voxel block along the principal axes [S1]. It serves as the first stage of SGGX parameter fitting, preceding the estimation of final self-shadowing probabilities [S1]. The method distinguishes between two variants: **Algorithm Iso**, which assumes isotropic self-shadowing ($A_0=1$), and **Algorithm Aniso**, which computes anisotropic self-shadowing parameters to exactly match the target transparencies [S1].
