 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- Division by zero: If the integral $\int D(m) \langle \omega_i \cdot m \rangle dm$ is zero for any axis, the density calculation is undefined. This may occur if the microflake distribution $D(m)$ has no support in the direction of the axis [S1].
-- Transparency values: $T(\omega_i)$ must be in the range $(0, 1]$. If $T(\omega_i) = 0$, $-\log(T(\omega_i))$ is infinite, leading to infinite density. If $T(\omega_i) = 1$, the density contribution is zero [S1].
